From: Gesher Authors
Subject: [PATCH] hwui: draw every frame posted to a surface the compositor does not consume

hwui drops a frame as AlreadyDrawn when its vsync time is within 2 ms of the
last swap's, so one frame is drawn per display vsync pulse. A Surface whose
consumer is not the display compositor (an ImageReader's, a SurfaceTexture's)
has no pulse to pace: Surface.lockHardwareCanvas gives each
unlockCanvasAndPost its own timestamp and its consumer expects a frame for
every post. Frames posted less than 2 ms after one another were dropped, with
no image and no onImageAvailable. A surface that does not queue to the window
composer (NATIVE_WINDOW_QUEUES_TO_WINDOW_COMPOSER is 0: Gesher's QueueSurface of
an ImageReader or a SurfaceTexture) is no longer subject to that skip. Window
surfaces are unchanged, and so is a SurfaceView's: its BLAST surface (also a
QueueSurface in Gesher) reports 1, as it does on Android where it is composited
into the window, and keeps the pacing.
---
diff --git a/libs/hwui/renderthread/CanvasContext.cpp b/libs/hwui/renderthread/CanvasContext.cpp
--- a/libs/hwui/renderthread/CanvasContext.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/renderthread/CanvasContext.cpp
@@ -519,7 +519,20 @@
         // the vsync was estimated due to being slow handling the signal.
         // See the logic in TimeLord#computeFrameTimeNanos or in
         // Choreographer.java for details on when this happens
+#ifdef GESHER
+        // Gesher: a vsync pulse paces frames shown by the display compositor. A
+        // surface whose consumer is not that compositor (an ImageReader or a
+        // SurfaceTexture, drawn with Surface.lockHardwareCanvas) takes every
+        // frame posted to it, so none is dropped for being soon after the last. A
        // SurfaceView's surface is composited into its window: it reports 1.
+        int queuesToComposer = 1;
+        ANativeWindow* const window = mNativeSurface ? mNativeSurface->getNativeWindow() : nullptr;
+        if (window != nullptr) {
+            window->query(window, NATIVE_WINDOW_QUEUES_TO_WINDOW_COMPOSER, &queuesToComposer);
+        }
+        if (vsyncDelta < 2_ms && queuesToComposer != 0) {
+#else
         if (vsyncDelta < 2_ms) {
+#endif
             // Already drew for this vsync pulse, UI draw request missed
             // the deadline for RT animations
             info.out.skippedFrameReason = SkippedFrameReason::AlreadyDrawn;
